      "writtenOn": "2026-01-30T20:12:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should keep only the excutable name and remove the path of it. I tested multiple corner cases, for instances:\n- Full path with arguments: \"/system/bin/ls /home/user -rlt\" → \"ls /home/user -rlt\"\n- Relative path: \"./test --arg1\" → \"test --arg1\"\n- Deeply nested binary: \"/vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.audio@2.0-service\" → \"android.hardware.audio@2.0-service\"\n- Kernel threads / Empty cmdline: cmdline is empty → keep as stat file, eg: \"kworker/3:0-events\"\n- Null-terminated argv: \"/system/bin/top\\0--arg1\\0--arg2\\0\\0\\0\\0\" → \"top --arg1 --arg2\"\n- Root directory executable: \"/init\" → \"init\"\n- Leading/Trailing whitespace: \" /system/bin/app \" → \"app\"\n- No arguments: \"/system/bin/sh\" → \"sh\"",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
